MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 075ae7a4e0c44354e9959697c9e269fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Homeland Security
  legacyName: Homeland Security
  description: "Cities gain +5 Defense, and the civilization gains +5% Espionage Defense."
  flavorText: "The crisis demonstrated that defense could no longer begin only at borders and battlefields. Transport networks, utilities, government buildings, communications systems, and crowded civilian spaces all became part of security planning. Intelligence services learned to share warnings before separate fragments of information became separate failures, while local authorities practiced protecting vulnerable sites without waiting for a conventional army to appear. The resulting system was less visible than a fortress wall but spread much farther. Security became an architecture of preparation woven through ordinary infrastructure."
  policyPointCost: 1
